<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">United States Bill of Rights</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1791">1791</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Bill of Rights is the first ten amendments to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">United States Constitution</a>, proposed by Congress in 1789 and ratified in 1791. Drafted largely by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-madison">James Madison</a> to answer Anti-Federalist fears of a strong central government, it guarantees freedom of religion, speech, the press and assembly, the right to bear arms and the rights of the accused, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jury-trial">trial by jury</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states-bill-of-rights.jpg" alt="United States Bill of Rights" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Archives and Records Administration. Office of the Federal Register. 4/1/1985 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bill_of_Rights_-_DPLA_-_a65f6d0b6210c18d17c596908ebcf270_(page_1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
